"I will first analyze each critical gap and flaw from the evaluator feedback. 1) Several functionalities from the source document are not explicitly covered: managing favorite clubs (add requirement), centralized dashboard/aggregation (add requirement), viewing all leagues/competitions (add requirement), explicit offline-to-online reconnection refresh (expand offline requirement), country determination for stream rights (expand/clarify requirement), full notifications for 'current events' (clarify/expand notification requirement), and clearly define guest vs authenticated usage model (add/clarify requirement). 2) Process requirements like 'undergo thorough testing' and 'ongoing feedback analysis' are not product requirements and will be removed. 3) Some acceptance criteria are vague or untestable ('promptly', 'comprehensive details', 'immediately', etc.); all BDDs will be rewritten for clear, measurable outcomes. 4) Architecture/implementation details (e.g., API/server) should not be user stories—move these to supporting requirements, not main user stories. 5) Requirement overlaps will be resolved: the live ticker feature will be unified for user-facing value, technical details referenced only as enabling constraints. 6) Any ambiguous or untestable phrases will be clarified, e.g., FR-008 ('interface extensions') rewritten or qualified. 7) Social sharing will be specified (link, summary, OS share sheet). 8) Country-based streaming logic and negative paths made explicit. 9) Duplication is avoided by refactoring live ticker and team/player info to explicitly cover offline and reconnection scenarios. 10) Platform NFR (NFR-001) will specify functional equivalency, not identicality. 11) Non-functional requirements needing testable thresholds (e.g., performance, GDPR) will be split or clarified. 12) All new or updated requirements will include both happy and negative path BDD scenarios as applicable. 13) Registration/login clarified for guest/required/optional features."